1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,837
[BILLY]<i> In a way,</i>
<i>I should actually thank you.</i>

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,757
<i>If you hadn't stolen LoveFeast,</i>

3
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:10,593
<i>I wouldn't have thought</i>
<i>of something much better.</i>

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:13,513
<i>Which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

5
00:00:13,596 --> 00:00:15,724
<i>Why don't you just tell the truth,</i>

6
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:18,727
<i>so I can understand</i>
<i>where your anger is coming from?</i>

7
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,064
<i>Your relationship with Caloy?</i>

8
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:26,401
<i>- We don't have a relationship.</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>You don't?</i>

9
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,197
<i>Hi, dude. Good morning!</i>

10
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,200
<i>Auntie Pres's birthday is coming up.</i>

11
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,744
<i>What's our plan?</i>

12
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,287
<i>Let's see.</i>

13
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>I'll get going.</i>
<i>I've got things to do.</i>

14
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,294
[BILLY] <i>Kris? Hi!</i>

15
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:45,628
<i>Oh, you're near?</i>

16
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,964
<i>Okay, I can meet you outside.</i>

17
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:49,883
<i>Yes. See you in a bit.</i>

18
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:53,970
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

19
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:04,189
<i>- Hi, Kris!</i>
<i>- Hi, Billy.</i>

20
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,983
<i>- Nice to finally meet you.</i>
<i>- Likewise.</i>

21
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,321
[BILLY] <i>What are you doing there?</i>

22
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:12,489
<i>I'm just taking a break.</i>

23
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>Okay. Um…</i>

24
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>Jordan, I want you to meet</i>
<i>Kristina Salintado.</i>

25
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,454
<i>She's an influencer.</i>

26
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,540
<i>- Jordan.</i>
<i>- Kris.</i>

27
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,917
<i>You're Kris.</i>

28
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,210
<i>Yes, Kris.</i>

29
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,712
<i>- Yes, nice to meet you.</i>
<i>- I thought…</i>

30
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,339
<i>Never mind.</i>

31
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:30,423
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

32
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,467
<i>- Kris.</i>
<i>- Kris, yes.</i>

33
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:33,426
<i>- She's Kris.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

34
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:37,764
<i>I don't know if it's right</i>
<i>to feel this way about Sir Eric.</i>

35
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:43,186
[LYDIA] <i>Then try Sir Eric too.</i>

36
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,938
<i>Just tell him how you feel.</i>

37
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:48,149
[PRECIOUS] <i>Oh, please. I don't even know</i>
<i>if what I'm feeling for Eric is right.</i>

38
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,902
[LYDIA] <i>Are you a teenager? Are you?</i>

39
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,113
<i>Are you still going to play hard to get?</i>

40
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:58,701
<i>Olive. Do I really have to stay away</i>
<i>from our children now?</i>

41
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:00,912
<i>I want to apologize to Billy,</i>

42
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:04,290
<i>but I don't want to make things</i>
<i>harder for her.</i>

43
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,710
<i>You can tell me anything.</i>

44
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:09,337
<i>Is it about your family?</i>

45
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:12,423
<i>If you're not ready to talk, that's fine.</i>

46
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:14,384
<i>Just know that I'm here for you, Sir Eric.</i>

47
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,302
<i>Just call me Eric.</i>

48
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:17,512
<i>Mm.</i>

49
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:20,640
<i>Okay. I'm here for you, Eric.</i>

50
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:23,143
[ENRICO] <i>Thanks for…</i>

51
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:25,019
<i>keeping me company.</i>

52
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,479
[PRECIOUS] <i>Don't mention it.</i>

53
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:28,898
<i>I just want to repay your kindness.</i>

54
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:32,694
<i>Dude. You know what</i>
<i>Auntie Pres would like?</i>

55
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,696
<i>- Hmm?</i>
<i>- Filipino food.</i>

56
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:37,240
<i>- That's her favorite.</i>
<i>- Correct.</i>

57
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:39,868
<i>It should be a Filipino restaurant.</i>
<i>I know the perfect place.</i>

58
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:41,953
<i>Auntie Pres is going to love it, I know.</i>

59
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:44,455
<i>Let me see. Oh, you're not sick anymore.</i>

60
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:46,499
<i>You're so happy and full of energy now.</i>

61
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,835
<i>- Huh?</i>
<i>- Good mood today, huh?</i>

62
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:50,128
<i>I wonder why.</i>

63
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:51,713
<i>You like her, don't you?</i>

64
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:54,215
<i>Kris?</i>

65
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,050
<i>- Mm.</i>
<i>- No.</i>

66
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:57,635
<i>Then why did you go downstairs earlier?</i>

67
00:02:57,719 --> 00:03:00,471
<i>You even went to greet her.</i>
<i>And you keep repeating her name.</i>

68
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,515
<i>- Mm? Mm? Mm?</i>
<i>- Dude! It's not like that.</i>

69
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:03,808
<i>- You got it all wrong.</i>
<i>- Oh, really?</i>

70
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:04,726
<i>- Me?</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

71
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,561
<i>- Fine, you don't like her.</i>
<i>- I thought…</i>

72
00:03:06,644 --> 00:03:07,604
<i>You like me.</i>

73
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:09,272
<i>- Huh?</i>
<i>- Me.</i>

74
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,441
<i>Whatever.</i>

75
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:12,525
<i>You're too gullible.</i>

76
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,152
<i>Come on. Back to work.</i>

77
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,330
Wow!

78
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:27,540
You're up early, Ms. Supervisor.

79
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:28,750
Are you leaving already?

80
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,877
Well, I have to.

81
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,256
I have a lot of work to do as supervisor.

82
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,174
Ah…

83
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,551
Well, if your sister were here,

84
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,720
she'd be proud of you.

85
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:43,264
You're successful, just like her.

86
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,225
- Hmm? Do your best, dear.
- [CHUCKLES]

87
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,769
I will, like I always do.

88
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:49,437
[MARIELA] All right, take care!

89
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:55,735
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:09,999
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

91
00:04:12,168 --> 00:04:13,586
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

92
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:19,759
Mm?

93
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:22,345
Why don't you look excited
about your leadership camp?

94
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,138
Oliver…

95
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:25,682
It's overnight, okay?

96
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,392
So don't forget your patch.

97
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:29,769
You're going with your classmates.

98
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:34,440
But it's on the same day
as Auntie's birthday.

99
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:36,734
You don't have to go if you don't want to.

100
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:40,738
But you'll have to write
a reflection paper instead.

101
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:43,533
But I really want to go, Billy.

102
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:45,118
I'm a student leader.

103
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,869
If I don't attend,

104
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:49,706
I might not get elected
student leader again next school year.

105
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:52,625
Oh, so that's what this is about.

106
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:57,672
But I don't want to miss
Auntie's birthday either.

107
00:04:57,755 --> 00:05:01,384
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,219
Auntie will understand.

109
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,055
We can always do a video call.

110
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:09,017
Then, we'll celebrate again
when you get back.

111
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,729
I know!

112
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:15,064
I'll just do a video call with her.

113
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:19,777
And… what would be
an awesome gift for Auntie?

114
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:23,781
Do you know what's the best birthday gift
you can give to Auntie?

115
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:26,200
Good grades.

116
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,911
That's the best gift
you can give Auntie Pres.

117
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:30,455
And to me too.

118
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:33,666
Okay, Billy. I'll do my best
at the student leadership camp!

119
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:39,630
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,757
Are you sure you want to go?

121
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,134
Yes! Sign it, please.

122
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,636
It has no ink.

123
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,514
All right, I'm signing it now.

124
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:54,103
- Thank you, Billy!
- One day without this rascal!

125
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,229
My goodness!

126
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:58,024
- Are you going to miss me?
- A bit.

127
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,942
- Just a bit?
- Don't forget your patch, okay?

128
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,694
- You'll miss me just a bit?
- And your medicine.

129
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,446
If there's a problem, call me immediately.

130
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:05,323
Your teachers already know. Okay?

131
00:06:05,406 --> 00:06:08,826
- You promise.
- Yes, I promise. I promise.

132
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,620
- Be good, okay?
- Yes.

133
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:12,497
- You'll miss me, right?
- Mm-hmm.

134
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,623
You promise?

135
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:21,714
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:10,972
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,474
[LINE RINGING]

138
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,226
Pres.

139
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:16,936
Do you have any plans later?

140
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,020
[PRECIOUS] Why?

141
00:07:19,605 --> 00:07:21,566
There's something I want to tell you.

142
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:24,527
[PRECIOUS] Huh? About what?

143
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:27,363
I want to tell you in person.

144
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,449
Can we meet?

145
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:33,244
Hmm… Okay. Sure.

146
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:38,166
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:39,625
[LINE RINGING]

148
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,502
[SQUEALING] Lydia!

149
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:43,671
I think he's planning to confess to me!

150
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:46,048
Yeah.

151
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:48,384
I didn't expect things would go this fast

152
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:51,012
after knowing each other
for only a few weeks.

153
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,305
[PRECIOUS] Yeah, Lydia.

154
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,557
<i>All right, all right.</i>

155
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,726
I'm done second-guessing!

156
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:58,811
I'm taking the risk!
[SQUEALS]

157
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:05,776
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:15,036
Dude, I already called the restaurant.

159
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:16,662
They want to know the headcount.

160
00:08:17,246 --> 00:08:18,748
Who are you inviting?

161
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:22,210
Probably the staff from Angels of Grace

162
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:24,754
and Auntie Pres's friends.

163
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:26,297
Okay.

164
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:29,133
So how are we setting this up?

165
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,801
I'll figure something out, dude.

166
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:34,514
But you're in charge
of the entertainment, okay?

167
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,140
[CHUCKLES] Leave it to me.

168
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:37,892
Anything for you.

169
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:41,729
Okay. Thank you.

170
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,357
- [KNOCKING ON DOOR]
- Auntie Pres is here.

171
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,942
- [PRECIOUS] Billy?
- I'll hang up now. Bye.

172
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:46,943
Yes, Auntie?

173
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:52,490
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,040
- Wow!
- Hm?

175
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:03,543
Wow!

176
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,336
- [CHUCKLES]
- You look beautiful!

177
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:06,629
Thank you.

178
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:08,339
Are you going somewhere?

179
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:11,300
Just going out to get some fresh air.

180
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:12,635
Nice.

181
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,429
Would you like me to get you a scarf?

182
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:17,306
- Yes. It may be too windy.
- Yeah.

183
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,767
[BOTH LAUGH]

184
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:22,103
Let me see…

185
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:26,023
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:28,276
Oh, this would look good
on you, Auntie Pres.

187
00:09:28,359 --> 00:09:30,069
- Yes.
- Oh!

188
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,612
- Sorry, Auntie Pres!
- Oh!

189
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,614
- Don't use that.
- Why?

190
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,783
- Wipe it off.
- Why?

191
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:39,078
- I forgot to throw it away.
- What's wrong with it?

192
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,831
This is from Mariela.

193
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:43,708
- Ugh! My goodness, Billy!
- Yeah.

194
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:44,959
[BILLY LAUGHS] Sorry.

195
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,502
Why'd you keep it?

196
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:49,171
I forgot to throw it away. I'm sorry.

197
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:52,008
Use this one instead. It's safe.

198
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:54,385
- Should I wash--?
- No, it's okay.

199
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:56,554
- What?
- You're good.

200
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:57,763
- My goodness.
- Here.

201
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:09,150
That's the right decision, Enrico.

202
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:13,946
You need to tell your children's
mother figure the truth about who you are.

203
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:17,450
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:21,621
I wouldn't really call Precious
a mother figure.

205
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:25,750
They see her as their real mother.

206
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,084
Oh.

207
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,503
All the more reason
why you should come clean.

208
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:32,006
It'll help lighten the burden
you're carrying.

209
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,383
Even if there's a chance

210
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:37,219
she'll get angry with me

211
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,555
and I won't get to see my children again?

212
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:43,768
What's important is that you're honest

213
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:45,811
with the person who loves them.

214
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:48,439
And with the woman you love.

215
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:53,444
You love Precious, don't you?

216
00:10:54,028 --> 00:11:00,910
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

217
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,543
How was work, dear?

218
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:11,462
Mm!

219
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:14,131
Exhausting, Ma.
I had so much to deal with.

220
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:15,883
There were so many screw-ups!

221
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:17,385
[LAUGHING]

222
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:21,180
My daughter really is amazing.

223
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,641
Come on, eat.

224
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:25,851
- I know you're hungry.
- Yes, Ma.

225
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:29,438
I cooked <i>sinigang.</i>

226
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:34,819
[WOMAN 1] <i>Sorry, Ms. Mercado,</i>
<i>but we can't process your application</i>

227
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,904
<i>without a police clearance.</i>

228
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:39,323
[WOMAN 2] <i>Miss, you have a pending case?</i>

229
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:42,493
[WOMAN 3] <i>We can't hire you, Ms. Mercado.</i>

230
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:46,622
<i>Your involvement with Carlos Toledo</i>
<i>is all over social media.</i>

231
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:50,918
<i>We don't accept applicants</i>
<i>with connections or ties to criminals.</i>

232
00:11:53,671 --> 00:12:00,553
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,689
Good evening, Chief.
Can you check these records?

234
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:19,822
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

235
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:23,868
It's all clear. Get him inside.

236
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:25,995
- Yes, sir. Thank you.
- Go ahead.

237
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:27,079
Let's go.

238
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:29,498
- Thank you, Chief.
- Take care on your way home.

239
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,876
Take good care of him.

240
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:37,006
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:41,927
[SHUTTERS CLICKING]

242
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:51,604
[MAN 1] Oh, fresh fish!

243
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:54,231
- Come on!
- Chief, put him here!

244
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:57,193
All of you, get some sleep.

245
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:58,527
[METAL DOOR CREAKS]

246
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,946
- [MAN 1] Chief, put him here!
- Hey, quiet down!

247
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,323
Get some sleep.

248
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:04,074
[MAN 2] Can we have him here?

249
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:08,329
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [MAN 3] I'll take care of you later.

250
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,455
[MAN 4] What?

251
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:10,706
[CHUCKLING]

252
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:14,210
Go ahead. Go to your bed.

253
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:17,421
[TALIA] <i>What are you doing here?</i>
<i>I thought you were in jail.</i>

254
00:13:17,505 --> 00:13:20,132
<i>What? I've done nothing wrong!</i>

255
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:22,718
<i>You were working together with that thief!</i>

256
00:13:22,801 --> 00:13:23,802
<i>No! That's not true!</i>

257
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,679
<i>- Whoever said that--</i>
<i>- Security, take her outside!</i>

258
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,306
<i>- Ms. Talia, I just need a job!</i>
<i>- Now, go!</i>

259
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:30,017
<i>- I'm begging you, Ms. Talia! Please!</i>
- [GUARD]<i> Please leave, ma'am.</i>

260
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,060
- [BEA] <i>Ms. Talia!</i>
<i>- Billy?</i>

261
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:33,854
<i>Bea's here and she's making a scene.</i>

262
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:36,857
<i>I thought our plan would put her in jail.</i>

263
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:41,320
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:43,531
